Subject: [PATCH v17 00/12] accel/rocket: RK3576 NPU (RKNN) enablement

This series adds RK3576 NPU (RKNN) support to the mainline DRM rocket
driver.

Based on: next-20261113

The pmdomain patches of v16 (9/16 and 10/16) are now a separate series on
Ulf's next. 12/12 needs its 2/3 to make the NPU domain take its supply:
https://lore.kernel.org/all/cover.1794615323.git.gahing@gahingwoo.com/

Changes in v17:

PLACEHOLDER(Jiaxing): Finley (v16 7/16, 10/16, 14/16 dropped), Heiko
(ROCKET_CLK_* in 1/12 and 9/12), the pmdomain split. See the key points.

Testing:

PLACEHOLDER(Jiaxing): what v17 was run on.

Known issue: after repeated resets with a 2 ms job timeout, the IOMMU
does not recover ("MMU_DTE_ADDR is not functioning"). I have not looked
into it further.

Tool use:

PLACEHOLDER(Jiaxing): the v16 paragraph, with "v16" changed to "v17".

Tag changes:

PLACEHOLDER(Jiaxing): Heiko's Reviewed-by on 1/12 (changed since);
Conor's Acked-by on 7/12; Tomeu's enum question on 10/12.

Igor Paunovic (1):
  accel/rocket: request the core clocks by name

Jiaxing Hu (11):
  accel/rocket: take the completion register writes under job_lock
  accel/rocket: wait for a running IRQ handler before resetting a core
  accel/rocket: let the core suspend after a reset
  accel/rocket: factor the completion tail out of the IRQ handler
  dt-bindings: npu: rockchip: add rockchip,rk3576-rknn-core
  dt-bindings: iommu: rockchip: describe the RK3576 NPU MMU
  accel/rocket: select the per-core clock and reset counts from match
    data
  accel/rocket: add RK3576 NPU (RKNN) support
  accel/rocket: add a GET_PARAM ioctl for the hardware version
  arm64: dts: rockchip: add NPU (RKNN) nodes to rk3576
  arm64: dts: rockchip: enable the NPU on rk3576-rock-4d

